# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formalism for the latest version of Qiskit noise learning"
msgstr "Formalisme matematik untuk versi terkini Qiskit noise learning"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formalism"
msgstr "Formalisme matematik"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formalism {#mathematical-formalism}"
msgstr "Formalisme matematik {#mathematical-formalism}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given the task of learning Pauli noise for a set of Clifford gates, a common analysis technique is to track how individual Pauli operators are transformed through a sequence of gate applications (under the assumption that the gates are Clifford and the noise is a Pauli channel, a single Pauli will always be mapped to another Pauli up to a scalar that is a function of the noise). Obviously, the evolution of *any* state under such a sequence can be captured by a linear combination of such trajectories, but under the assumption that we always prepare the state in a Pauli eigenstate, and always measure and post-process the results to compute the expectation value of a Pauli operator, the relationship between the expectation value and the noise model parameters will *always* depend on only a single such trajectory. This follows from the simple fact that the initial state is a linear combination of Pauli operators, each gate and noise model maps Paulis to Paulis and preserves their orthogonality, and the final expectation value “selects” only one of the Paulis in the final decomposition before measurement.\n"
msgstr "Diberi tugas mempelajari hingar Pauli bagi satu set gate Clifford, teknik analisis yang lazim ialah menjejak bagaimana pengendali Pauli individu diubah melalui satu jujukan penggunaan gate (dengan andaian bahawa gate tersebut ialah Clifford dan hingar ialah saluran Pauli, satu Pauli akan sentiasa dipetakan kepada Pauli lain sehingga satu skalar yang merupakan fungsi hingar). Jelas sekali, evolusi *sebarang* keadaan di bawah jujukan sedemikian boleh ditangkap oleh gabungan linear trajektori sedemikian, tetapi di bawah andaian bahawa kita sentiasa menyediakan keadaan dalam keadaan eigen Pauli, dan sentiasa mengukur serta memproses pasca keputusan untuk mengira nilai jangkaan pengendali Pauli, hubungan antara nilai jangkaan dan parameter model hingar akan *sentiasa* bergantung pada hanya satu trajektori sedemikian. Ini terhasil daripada fakta mudah bahawa keadaan awal ialah gabungan linear pengendali Pauli, setiap gate dan model hingar memetakan Pauli kepada Pauli serta mengekalkan ortogonaliti mereka, dan nilai jangkaan akhir “memilih” hanya satu daripada Pauli dalam penguraian akhir sebelum pengukuran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This type of reasoning appears in many parallel research tracks in noise learning, including in the Pauli gate-set learning literature \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\"), [2](#id20 \"Edward H. Chen, Senrui Chen, Laurin E. Fischer, Andrew Eddins, Luke C. G. Govia, Brad Mitchell, Andre He, Youngseok Kim, Liang Jiang, and Alireza Seif. Disambiguating pauli noise in quantum computers. PRX Quantum, pages, 2026. doi:10.1103/69wc-gzl6.\")], the ACES literature \\[[3](#id15 \"Steven T. Flammia. Averaged Circuit Eigenvalue Sampling. In 17th Conference on the Theory of Quantum Computation, Communication and Cryptography (TQC 2022), volume 232 of Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs), 4:1–4:10. Dagstuhl, Germany, 2022. Schloss Dagstuhl – Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik. doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.TQC.2022.4.\")], and the cycle benchmarking literature \\[[4](#id14 \"Alexander Erhard, Joel J. Wallman, Lukas Postler, Michael Meth, Roman Stricker, Esteban A. Martinez, Philipp Schindler, Thomas Monz, Joseph Emerson, and Rainer Blatt. Characterizing large-scale quantum computers via cycle benchmarking. Nature Communications, 10(1):5347, 2019. doi:10.1038/s41467-019-13068-7.\")]. This reasoning was further generalized in \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] to include Clifford-MCM gates (a Clifford gate followed by a projective mid-circuit measurement). This package most closely follows \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\"), [5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")]. While not explicitly named, we adopt the *Pattern Transfer Graph* (PTG) formalism for describing how Pauli operators evolve through learning circuits, providing a direct data representation of *paths* through the graph.\n"
msgstr "Jenis penaakulan ini muncul dalam banyak laluan penyelidikan selari dalam pembelajaran hingar, termasuk dalam literatur pembelajaran set gate Pauli \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\"), [2](#id20 \"Edward H. Chen, Senrui Chen, Laurin E. Fischer, Andrew Eddins, Luke C. G. Govia, Brad Mitchell, Andre He, Youngseok Kim, Liang Jiang, and Alireza Seif. Disambiguating pauli noise in quantum computers. PRX Quantum, pages, 2026. doi:10.1103/69wc-gzl6.\")], literatur ACES \\[[3](#id15 \"Steven T. Flammia. Averaged Circuit Eigenvalue Sampling. In 17th Conference on the Theory of Quantum Computation, Communication and Cryptography (TQC 2022), volume 232 of Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs), 4:1–4:10. Dagstuhl, Germany, 2022. Schloss Dagstuhl – Leibniz-Zentrum für Informatik. doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.TQC.2022.4.\")], dan literatur penanda aras kitaran \\[[4](#id14 \"Alexander Erhard, Joel J. Wallman, Lukas Postler, Michael Meth, Roman Stricker, Esteban A. Martinez, Philipp Schindler, Thomas Monz, Joseph Emerson, and Rainer Blatt. Characterizing large-scale quantum computers via cycle benchmarking. Nature Communications, 10(1):5347, 2019. doi:10.1038/s41467-019-13068-7.\")]. Penaakulan ini telah digeneralisasikan lagi dalam \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] untuk merangkumi gate Clifford-MCM (gate Clifford diikuti pengukuran unjuran pertengahan litar). Pakej ini paling hampir mengikuti \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\"), [5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")]. Walaupun tidak dinamakan secara jelas, kami menggunakan formalisme *Pattern Transfer Graph* (PTG) untuk menerangkan bagaimana pengendali Pauli berevolusi melalui litar pembelajaran, yang menyediakan perwakilan data langsung bagi *laluan* melalui graf tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following is a review of some core mathematical concepts from the literature. It is primarily meant to consolidate notation, and to serve as a conceptual documentation reference for the rest of the package.\n"
msgstr "Berikut ialah ulasan beberapa konsep matematik teras daripada literatur. Ia terutamanya bertujuan untuk menyatukan tatatanda, dan berfungsi sebagai rujukan dokumentasi konseptual untuk bahagian pakej yang lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"background\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Background {#1-background}"
msgstr "1. Latar belakang {#1-background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"notation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.1 Notation {#11-notation}"
msgstr "1.1 Tatatanda {#11-notation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For $K \\in \\mathbb{N}$, let $[K] = \\{0, 1, \\dots, K - 1\\}$. For a finite set $S \\subset \\mathbb{N}$ of qubit indices, let $\\mathcal{P}^S$ denote the set of *unphased* Pauli operators acting on those qubits. Note that we think of elements of $\\mathcal{P}^S$ as functions mapping $S \\rightarrow \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}$, so that for any $P \\in \\mathcal{P}^S$ and $T \\subseteq S$, $P|_T$ denotes the restriction of $P$ to the qubit subset $T$. Along these lines, for disjoint sets $S, T$, and $P \\in \\mathcal{P}^S$ and $Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^T$, $P \\otimes Q$ denotes the element of $\\mathcal{P}^{S \\cup T}$ such that $P \\otimes Q |_S = P$ and $P \\otimes Q |_T = Q$. This notation is helpful to avoid explicitly dealing with subsystem orderings, and to make it easy to describe restrictions.\n"
msgstr "Untuk $K \\in \\mathbb{N}$, biarkan $[K] = \\{0, 1, \\dots, K - 1\\}$. Untuk set terhingga $S \\subset \\mathbb{N}$ bagi indeks qubit, biarkan $\\mathcal{P}^S$ menandakan set pengendali Pauli *tanpa fasa* yang bertindak pada qubit tersebut. Perhatikan bahawa kita menganggap unsur $\\mathcal{P}^S$ sebagai fungsi yang memetakan $S \\rightarrow \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}$, supaya bagi sebarang $P \\in \\mathcal{P}^S$ dan $T \\subseteq S$, $P|_T$ menandakan sekatan $P$ kepada subset qubit $T$. Selaras dengan itu, bagi set tak bersilang $S, T$, dan $P \\in \\mathcal{P}^S$ serta $Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^T$, $P \\otimes Q$ menandakan unsur $\\mathcal{P}^{S \\cup T}$ sedemikian rupa sehingga $P \\otimes Q |_S = P$ dan $P \\otimes Q |_T = Q$. Tatatanda ini berguna untuk mengelakkan pengendalian secara jelas susunan subsistem, dan memudahkan penerangan sekatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For finite subsets $M \\subset \\mathbb{N}$, we denote $\\mathbb{Z}_2^M$ as the set of the bit strings whose elements are indexed by $M$. Similarly to the above, we think of elements as functions mapping $M \\rightarrow \\mathbb{Z}_2$, so that we may easily describe substrings in terms of restrictions of the index set.\n"
msgstr "Bagi subset terhingga $M \\subset \\mathbb{N}$, kita menandakan $\\mathbb{Z}_2^M$ sebagai set rentetan bit yang unsurnya diindeks oleh $M$. Sama seperti di atas, kita menganggap unsur sebagai fungsi yang memetakan $M \\rightarrow \\mathbb{Z}_2$, supaya kita dapat menerangkan subrentetan dengan mudah dari segi sekatan set indeks.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lastly, for a matrix $X$, we use $| X \\rangle\\!\\rangle$ to denote its vectorization. Based on the limited way in which we use this notation, it is not actually necessary to choose a specific vectorization convention. For a classical bit string $m$, we use the shorthand $| m \\rangle\\!\\rangle = | | m \\rangle\\langle m | \\rangle\\!\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, bagi matriks $X$, kita menggunakan $| X \\rangle\\!\\rangle$ untuk menandakan pemvektorannya. Berdasarkan cara terhad kita menggunakan tatatanda ini, sebenarnya tidak perlu memilih konvensyen pemvektoran tertentu. Bagi rentetan bit klasik $m$, kita menggunakan singkatan $| m \\rangle\\!\\rangle = | | m \\rangle\\langle m | \\rangle\\!\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"quantum-instruments\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.2 Quantum instruments {#12-quantum-instruments}"
msgstr "1.2 Instrumen kuantum {#12-quantum-instruments}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A quantum operation producing classical bits $m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$ (for example, the result of measurement) is generally modeled as a linear map of the form:\n"
msgstr "Operasi kuantum yang menghasilkan bit klasik $m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$ (contohnya, hasil pengukuran) secara amnya dimodelkan sebagai peta linear berbentuk:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
" \\rho \\mapsto \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m(\\rho) \\otimes | m \\rangle\\langle m |, \n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
" \\rho \\mapsto \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m(\\rho) \\otimes | m \\rangle\\langle m |, \n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the set $\\{\\mathcal{E}_m: m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M\\}$ are completely positive, and $\\sum_m \\mathcal{E}_m$ is trace-preserving. A set of completely positive maps $\\{\\mathcal{E}_m\\}$ satisfying these properties is called a *quantum instrument*. A unitary gate is a special case of an instrument with only one element that is a unitary operation.\n"
msgstr "di mana set $\\{\\mathcal{E}_m: m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M\\}$ adalah positif sepenuhnya, dan $\\sum_m \\mathcal{E}_m$ mengekalkan surih. Satu set peta positif sepenuhnya $\\{\\mathcal{E}_m\\}$ yang memenuhi sifat ini dipanggil *instrumen kuantum*. Gate uniter ialah kes khas instrumen dengan hanya satu unsur yang merupakan operasi uniter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"noisy-clifford-mcm-reset-gates\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Noisy Clifford-MCM-reset gates {#2-noisy-clifford-mcm-reset-gates}"
msgstr "2. Gate Clifford-MCM-reset yang bising {#2-noisy-clifford-mcm-reset-gates}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The formalism utilized in this package assumes every gate in the gate set to be characterized consists of the following sequence of operations on $K$ qubits:\n"
msgstr "Formalisme yang digunakan dalam pakej ini mengandaikan setiap gate dalam set gate yang hendak dicirikan terdiri daripada jujukan operasi berikut pada $K$ qubit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Clifford operation on all qubits.\n"
msgstr "Operasi Clifford pada semua qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A mid-circuit projective measurement along $Z$ on some subset of qubits $M \\subseteq [K]$.\n"
msgstr "Pengukuran unjuran pertengahan litar sepanjang $Z$ pada sesetengah subset qubit $M \\subseteq [K]$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A mid-circuit reset to the $Z$ ground state on some subset of qubits $R \\subseteq [K]$.\n"
msgstr "Set semula pertengahan litar kepada keadaan dasar $Z$ pada sesetengah subset qubit $R \\subseteq [K]$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a general class of operations that includes unitary Clifford gates, measurement, state preparation, and any combination of the above. Note that we assume measurement and reset are always along the $Z$-axis for each qubit. While this is not strictly required, it is a common feature of many quantum computing modalities, and enables simplified representations and analysis.\n"
msgstr "Ini ialah kelas operasi am yang merangkumi gate Clifford uniter, pengukuran, penyediaan keadaan, dan sebarang gabungan di atas. Perhatikan bahawa kita mengandaikan pengukuran dan set semula sentiasa sepanjang paksi $Z$ bagi setiap qubit. Walaupun ini tidak diwajibkan secara ketat, ia ialah ciri lazim bagi banyak modaliti pengkomputeran kuantum, dan membolehkan perwakilan serta analisis yang dipermudah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As outlined in \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\"), [6](#id18 \"Stefanie J. Beale and Joel J. Wallman. Randomized compiling for subsystem measurements. 2023. URL: http://arxiv.org/abs/2304.06599, doi:10.48550/arXiv.2304.06599.\")] for the no-reset case, if a specific twirling strategy is applied to a noisy instance of such a gate, then the action of the resulting operation can be modeled mathematically as a *uniform Pauli instrument*. That is, within the quantum instrument notation, $\\mathcal{E}_m = \\mathcal{U}_mG$, where $G$ is the Clifford unitary, and:\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang digariskan dalam \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\"), [6](#id18 \"Stefanie J. Beale and Joel J. Wallman. Randomized compiling for subsystem measurements. 2023. URL: http://arxiv.org/abs/2304.06599, doi:10.48550/arXiv.2304.06599.\")] bagi kes tanpa set semula, jika strategi twirling tertentu dikenakan pada satu instans gate sedemikian yang bising, maka tindakan operasi yang terhasil boleh dimodelkan secara matematik sebagai *instrumen Pauli seragam*. Iaitu, dalam tatatanda instrumen kuantum, $\\mathcal{E}_m = \\mathcal{U}_mG$, di mana $G$ ialah uniter Clifford, dan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
" \\mathcal{U}_m = \\sum_{a,b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\Lambda_{a,b} \\otimes | m + a \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle m + b |, \n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
" \\mathcal{U}_m = \\sum_{a,b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\Lambda_{a,b} \\otimes | m + a \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle m + b |, \n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where each $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ is a sub-normalized Pauli channel on the unmeasured qubits $N = [K] \\setminus M$. It is implied by this being a quantum instrument that $\\sum_{a,b} \\Lambda_{a,b}$ is also trace-preserving. Some notes:\n"
msgstr "di mana setiap $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ ialah saluran Pauli sub-ternormal pada qubit yang tidak diukur $N = [K] \\setminus M$. Ia tersirat daripada ini sebagai instrumen kuantum bahawa $\\sum_{a,b} \\Lambda_{a,b}$ juga mengekalkan surih. Beberapa nota:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The initial untwirled noise is modeled to include both “quantum” and “classical” errors: erroneous operations on the quantum registers, as well as mistakes in the measurement value reporting.\n"
msgstr "Hingar awal yang tidak di-twirl dimodelkan merangkumi ralat “kuantum” dan “klasik”: operasi yang salah pada daftar kuantum, serta kesilapan dalam pelaporan nilai pengukuran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The noise map $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ is *independent* of the measurement outcome $m$.\n"
msgstr "Peta hingar $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ *tidak bergantung* pada hasil pengukuran $m$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In words, a single term in the above sum represents observing a measurement outcome of $m$ when the measured state was $| m + b \\rangle$ (a misclassification if $b \\neq 0$), and when the output state on the measurement register is $| m + a \\rangle$ (the “wrong” state when $a \\neq 0$). The map $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ simultaneously encodes the action on the unmeasured qubits (conditioned on the measurement behavior) and the *probability* of the specific measurement behavior (through the normalization).\n"
msgstr "Dengan kata lain, satu sebutan dalam hasil tambah di atas mewakili pemerhatian hasil pengukuran $m$ apabila keadaan yang diukur ialah $| m + b \\rangle$ (salah klasifikasi jika $b \\neq 0$), dan apabila keadaan output pada daftar pengukuran ialah $| m + a \\rangle$ (keadaan yang “salah” apabila $a \\neq 0$). Peta $\\Lambda_{a,b}$ secara serentak mengekod tindakan pada qubit yang tidak diukur (bersyarat pada tingkah laku pengukuran) dan *kebarangkalian* tingkah laku pengukuran tertentu (melalui penormalan).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that we are not concerned here with the specifics of the twirling strategy: that such a strategy exists to put the channel into the above form is enough. Note that “finer” twirling strategies exist which can further restrict the form of the Pauli channels \\[[7](#id19 \"Ewout van den Berg and Pawel Wocjan. Techniques for learning sparse Pauli-Lindblad noise models. Quantum, 8:1556, 2024. URL: https://quantum-journal.org/papers/q-2024-12-10-1556/, doi:10.22331/q-2024-12-10-1556.\")]; however, we take the above form as the most general mathematical representation under consideration.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa kita tidak mengambil kira butiran strategi twirling di sini: cukuplah bahawa strategi sedemikian wujud untuk meletakkan saluran dalam bentuk di atas. Perhatikan bahawa strategi twirling yang “lebih halus” wujud yang dapat mengehadkan lagi bentuk saluran Pauli \\[[7](#id19 \"Ewout van den Berg and Pawel Wocjan. Techniques for learning sparse Pauli-Lindblad noise models. Quantum, 8:1556, 2024. URL: https://quantum-journal.org/papers/q-2024-12-10-1556/, doi:10.22331/q-2024-12-10-1556.\")]; namun, kita mengambil bentuk di atas sebagai perwakilan matematik paling am yang dipertimbangkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Lemma 1 of \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")], it is shown that $\\mathcal{E}_m = \\mathcal{U}_mG$ can be rewritten as:\n"
msgstr "Dalam Lemma 1 \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")], ditunjukkan bahawa $\\mathcal{E}_m = \\mathcal{U}_mG$ boleh ditulis semula sebagai:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"equation-clifford-mcm-form\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
" \\mathcal{E}_m = \\frac{1}{2^{2|M| + |N|}}\\sum_{x, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^N} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y)}\n"
"\\lambda^Q_{x, y}| Q \\otimes Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes Z^x) |. \n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
" \\mathcal{E}_m = \\frac{1}{2^{2|M| + |N|}}\\sum_{x, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^N} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y)}\n"
"\\lambda^Q_{x, y}| Q \\otimes Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes Z^x) |. \n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for some real numbers $\\lambda_{x,y}^Q$, which are called the *fidelities* of the instrument.\n"
msgstr "untuk sesetengah nombor nyata $\\lambda_{x,y}^Q$, yang dipanggil *fidelity* instrumen tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding reset to this picture is relatively straightforward. A noisy reset operation on qubits $R \\subset [K]$ can be modeled according to the decomposition:\n"
msgstr "Menambahkan set semula pada gambaran ini agak mudah. Operasi set semula yang bising pada qubit $R \\subset [K]$ boleh dimodelkan mengikut penguraian:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"equation-reset-form\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
" \\frac{1}{2^{|R|}}\\sum_{r \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{R}} \\lambda_r | Z^r \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle I_R |. \n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
" \\frac{1}{2^{|R|}}\\sum_{r \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{R}} \\lambda_r | Z^r \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle I_R |. \n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The above form explicitly utilizes the assumption that the reset is along the $Z$-axis for each qubit. Noise in the operation is encoded in the reset fidelities $\\lambda_r$, which are simply indexed by qubit subsets.\n"
msgstr "Bentuk di atas secara jelas menggunakan andaian bahawa set semula adalah sepanjang paksi $Z$ bagi setiap qubit. Hingar dalam operasi dikodkan dalam fidelity set semula $\\lambda_r$, yang hanya diindeks oleh subset qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An analog to Equation [(1)](#equation-clifford-mcm-form) that includes a reset operation at the end can be attained by simply composing it with Equation [(2)](#equation-reset-form). This composition, after some simplification, yields:\n"
msgstr "Analog kepada Persamaan [(1)](#equation-clifford-mcm-form) yang merangkumi operasi set semula di hujung boleh diperoleh dengan hanya mengkomposisikannya dengan Persamaan [(2)](#equation-reset-form). Komposisi ini, selepas sedikit permudahan, menghasilkan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split} \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}} \\sum_{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ Q \\in\n"
"\\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y|_M)} \\lambda^Q_{x,y}  | Q \\otimes\n"
"Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |. \\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split} \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}} \\sum_{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ Q \\in\n"
"\\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y|_M)} \\lambda^Q_{x,y}  | Q \\otimes\n"
"Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |. \\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This decomposition indicates that the number of fidelities $\\lambda^Q_{x, y}$ is\n"
msgstr "Penguraian ini menunjukkan bahawa bilangan fidelity $\\lambda^Q_{x, y}$ ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"equation-num-fidelities\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"4^{|N \\setminus R|} 2^{|M|}2^{|M \\cup R|} = 4^{K}2^{|M|}2^{-|M \\cup R|} = 4^K 2^{-|R \\setminus M|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"4^{|N \\setminus R|} 2^{|M|}2^{|M \\cup R|} = 4^{K}2^{|M|}2^{-|M \\cup R|} = 4^K 2^{-|R \\setminus M|}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider limiting cases: (1) For no measurement or reset, $M = R = \\emptyset$, and the expression yields $4^K$, the number of phase-less Pauli operators on $K$ qubits. (2) For $M = \\emptyset$ and $R=[K]$, this yields $2^K$, which is the number of subsets of $[K]$. Lastly, (3) for $M = [K]$ and $R = \\emptyset$, this yields $4^K$. Note that this may initially seem surprising: for standard learning, measurement and reset are typically considered to have the same number of fidelities: $2^K$. However, here the all-measurement gate in this context is understood not as a *terminal* measurement, but as an MCM, and as such fidelities corresponding to non-identity *outputs* of the measurement are also included (such as $y \\neq 0$ in Equation [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form)).\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan kes-kes had: (1) Bagi tiada pengukuran atau set semula, $M = R = \\emptyset$, dan ungkapan menghasilkan $4^K$, bilangan pengendali Pauli tanpa fasa pada $K$ qubit. (2) Bagi $M = \\emptyset$ dan $R=[K]$, ini menghasilkan $2^K$, iaitu bilangan subset $[K]$. Akhir sekali, (3) bagi $M = [K]$ dan $R = \\emptyset$, ini menghasilkan $4^K$. Perhatikan bahawa ini pada mulanya mungkin mengejutkan: bagi pembelajaran piawai, pengukuran dan set semula lazimnya dianggap mempunyai bilangan fidelity yang sama: $2^K$. Walau bagaimanapun, di sini gate semua-pengukuran dalam konteks ini difahami bukan sebagai pengukuran *terminal*, tetapi sebagai MCM, dan oleh itu fidelity yang sepadan dengan *output* pengukuran bukan identiti juga disertakan (seperti $y \\neq 0$ dalam Persamaan [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, it is important to note that any twirling strategy yielding the form in Equation [(1)](#equation-clifford-mcm-form) in the non-reset case still applies equally well to the non-trivial reset case with a simple modification. The potential problem is that such a twirling strategy may require operations on measured qubits *after* the measurement. Therefore, if a qubit is measured *and* reset, implementing the strategy seemingly requires inserting operations *within* the gate between the measurement and reset. However, given the nature of reset, any such operations have no effect, and can simply be skipped while still yielding the same desired structure.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, penting untuk diperhatikan bahawa sebarang strategi twirling yang menghasilkan bentuk dalam Persamaan [(1)](#equation-clifford-mcm-form) dalam kes tanpa set semula masih terpakai sama baik pada kes set semula yang tidak remeh dengan pengubahsuaian mudah. Masalah yang berpotensi ialah strategi twirling sedemikian mungkin memerlukan operasi pada qubit yang diukur *selepas* pengukuran. Oleh itu, jika qubit diukur *dan* di-set semula, pelaksanaan strategi tersebut nampaknya memerlukan pemasukan operasi *di dalam* gate antara pengukuran dan set semula. Walau bagaimanapun, memandangkan sifat set semula, sebarang operasi sedemikian tidak memberi kesan, dan boleh dilangkau sambil masih menghasilkan struktur yang dikehendaki.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"path-formalism\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Path formalism {#3-path-formalism}"
msgstr "3. Formalisme laluan {#3-path-formalism}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As described in the introduction, all learning algorithms for Pauli-type noise on Clifford gates are based around tracking how individual Paulis evolve through a circuit, picking up noise fidelity factors along the way. The expectation values of a circuit composed of such gates are therefore related simply to products of the underlying fidelities of the individual gates, and in this way model parameters can be inferred by *inverting* whatever sparse parameter-to-fidelity mapping is being assumed.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang diterangkan dalam pengenalan, semua algoritma pembelajaran bagi hingar jenis Pauli pada gate Clifford berasaskan penjejakan bagaimana Pauli individu berevolusi melalui litar, sambil mengumpul faktor fidelity hingar di sepanjang jalan. Nilai jangkaan bagi litar yang terdiri daripada gate sedemikian oleh itu berkait secara mudah dengan hasil darab fidelity asas bagi gate individu, dan dengan cara ini parameter model boleh disimpulkan dengan *menyongsangkan* apa-apa pemetaan parameter-ke-fidelity jarang yang diandaikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\")], in the context of unitary gate sets, this is formalized into the *Pattern Transfer Graph* (PTG): a directed graph describing all possible experiments consisting of elements of the gate set and layers of single-qubit Clifford gates (assumed to be perfect, or “free”, operations). This was generalized in \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] to include gate sets with mid-circuit measurements. In both cases, each experiment is described by tracking a single Pauli operator through the circuit, under the assumption of a particular observable being computed at each measurement site. Here we do not directly review the graph or path constructions; however, we present the required facts for justifying them within our own notation and with resets included.\n"
msgstr "Dalam \\[[1](#id17 \"Senrui Chen, Zhihan Zhang, Liang Jiang, and Steven T. Flammia. Efficient Self-Consistent Learning of Gate Set Pauli Noise. PRX Quantum, 7(1):010305, 2026. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/1pnv-t9px, doi:10.1103/1pnv-t9px.\")], dalam konteks set gate uniter, ini diformalkan menjadi *Pattern Transfer Graph* (PTG): graf terarah yang menerangkan semua eksperimen yang mungkin yang terdiri daripada unsur set gate dan lapisan gate Clifford qubit tunggal (dianggap operasi yang sempurna, atau “percuma”). Ini telah digeneralisasikan dalam \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] untuk merangkumi set gate dengan pengukuran pertengahan litar. Dalam kedua-dua kes, setiap eksperimen diterangkan dengan menjejak satu pengendali Pauli melalui litar, di bawah andaian satu observabel tertentu dikira pada setiap tapak pengukuran. Di sini kami tidak mengulas secara langsung pembinaan graf atau laluan; namun, kami membentangkan fakta yang diperlukan untuk mewajarkannya dalam tatatanda kami sendiri dan dengan set semula disertakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While the tracking of a single Pauli operator through the circuit may be intuitive in the unitary gate set case, it does not so obviously hold in the more general Clifford-MCM-reset case, due to the non-deterministic nature of measurement. The following proposition recovers this picture even in the more general case \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")]:\n"
msgstr "Walaupun penjejakan satu pengendali Pauli melalui litar mungkin intuitif dalam kes set gate uniter, ia tidak semestinya jelas berlaku dalam kes Clifford-MCM-reset yang lebih am, disebabkan sifat pengukuran yang tidak deterministik. Proposisi berikut memulihkan gambaran ini walaupun dalam kes yang lebih am \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")]:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Proposition 1\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  <span id=\"proof-content\" />\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Proposisi 1\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  <span id=\"proof-content\" />\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  For any $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$, $y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R}$, and $Q\\in \\mathcal{P}^{N \\setminus R}$, it holds that:\n"
msgstr "  Bagi sebarang $x \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$, $y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R}$, dan $Q\\in \\mathcal{P}^{N \\setminus R}$, berlaku bahawa:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\n"
msgstr "$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y |\\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} |_M \\left(\\sum_{m\\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\right)\n"
"= \\lambda_{x,y}^Q\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y |\\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} |_M \\left(\\sum_{m\\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\right)\n"
"= \\lambda_{x,y}^Q\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In other words, if we compute the expectation value $Z^{x + y|_M}$ on the classical register output by the MCM, then the “Heisenberg picture” evolution of an observable through the Clifford-MCM-reset gate maps $Q \\otimes Z^y \\rightarrow Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x$. This fact alone enables recovery of PTG-like analysis beyond the unitary gate set case: with a particular post-processing of the measurement results, even gates with measurements and resets can be viewed as deterministically mapping one Pauli operator to another.\n"
msgstr "Dengan kata lain, jika kita mengira nilai jangkaan $Z^{x + y|_M}$ pada daftar klasik yang dikeluarkan oleh MCM, maka evolusi “gambaran Heisenberg” suatu observabel melalui gate Clifford-MCM-reset memetakan $Q \\otimes Z^y \\rightarrow Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x$. Fakta ini sahaja membolehkan pemulihan analisis seperti PTG melangkaui kes set gate uniter: dengan pemprosesan pasca tertentu bagi keputusan pengukuran, malah gate dengan pengukuran dan set semula boleh dilihat sebagai memetakan satu pengendali Pauli kepada yang lain secara deterministik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before proving this, we write Equation [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form) in a more suggestive way. Note that for $x, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$, it holds that $Z^{x+y} = \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y)}| m \\rangle\\langle m |$, and as such (in super operator notation) we have:\n"
msgstr "Sebelum membuktikan ini, kita menulis Persamaan [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form) dengan cara yang lebih mencadangkan. Perhatikan bahawa bagi $x, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M$, berlaku $Z^{x+y} = \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} (-1)^{m \\cdot (x + y)}| m \\rangle\\langle m |$, dan oleh itu (dalam tatatanda superpengendali) kita mempunyai:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split} \\begin{aligned} \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle_M = \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}}\\sum_{\\substack{x \\in\n"
"\\mathbb{Z}_2^M, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} \\lambda^Q_{x,y}  | Q \\otimes Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\n"
"\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) | \\otimes | Z^{x + y|_M} \\rangle\\!\\rangle_M, \\end{aligned} \\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split} \\begin{aligned} \\sum_{m \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle_M = \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}}\\sum_{\\substack{x \\in\n"
"\\mathbb{Z}_2^M, y \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ Q \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} \\lambda^Q_{x,y}  | Q \\otimes Z^y \\rangle\\!\\rangle\n"
"\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) | \\otimes | Z^{x + y|_M} \\rangle\\!\\rangle_M, \\end{aligned} \\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where we have applied Equation [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form) and collected terms, and we use the subscript $M$ to indicate the classical measurement result register, which we treat above in a similar notation to the quantum registers.\n"
msgstr "di mana kita telah menggunakan Persamaan [(3)](#equation-clifford-mcm-reset-form) dan mengumpulkan sebutan, dan kita menggunakan subskrip $M$ untuk menandakan daftar hasil pengukuran klasik, yang kita layan di atas dalam tatatanda yang serupa dengan daftar kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Proof. It holds that:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Bukti. Berlaku bahawa:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y | \\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} | \\left(\\sum_{m\\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\right)\\\\\n"
"&= \\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y | \\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} | \\left( \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}} \\sum_{\\substack{a \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ P \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} \\lambda^P_{a,b}  | P \\otimes Z^b \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(P \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^a) | \\otimes | Z^{a + b|_M} \\rangle\\!\\rangle \\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{1}{2^{2|M| + |N|}}\\sum_{\\substack{a \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ P \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N \\setminus R}}} \\lambda^P_{a, b}\\underbrace{\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y, P \\otimes Z^b \\rangle}_{2^{|M| + |N|} \\delta_{P, Q}\\delta_{y,b}} \\underbrace{\\langle Z^{x + y|_M}, Z^{a + b|_M} \\rangle}_{2^{|M|}\\delta_{x+y|_M,a+b|_M}}\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(P \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^a) |\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y | \\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} | \\left(\\sum_{m\\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M} \\mathcal{E}_m \\otimes | m \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\right)\\\\\n"
"&= \\langle\\!\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y | \\otimes \\langle\\!\\langle Z^{x + y|_M} | \\left( \\frac{1}{2^{2|M|+|N|}} \\sum_{\\substack{a \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ P \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N\\setminus R}}} \\lambda^P_{a,b}  | P \\otimes Z^b \\rangle\\!\\rangle\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(P \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^a) | \\otimes | Z^{a + b|_M} \\rangle\\!\\rangle \\right) \\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{1}{2^{2|M| + |N|}}\\sum_{\\substack{a \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^M, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^{M \\cup R} \\\\ P \\in \\mathcal{P}^{N \\setminus R}}} \\lambda^P_{a, b}\\underbrace{\\langle Q \\otimes Z^y, P \\otimes Z^b \\rangle}_{2^{|M| + |N|} \\delta_{P, Q}\\delta_{y,b}} \\underbrace{\\langle Z^{x + y|_M}, Z^{a + b|_M} \\rangle}_{2^{|M|}\\delta_{x+y|_M,a+b|_M}}\\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(P \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^a) |\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Lastly, observe that $\\delta_{y,b}\\delta_{x+y|_M,a+b|_M} = \\delta_{y,b}\\delta_{x,a}$, and hence the final term above collapses down to the single term $\\lambda^Q_{x,y} \\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |$, yielding the desired result.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Akhir sekali, perhatikan bahawa $\\delta_{y,b}\\delta_{x+y|_M,a+b|_M} = \\delta_{y,b}\\delta_{x,a}$, dan oleh itu sebutan akhir di atas runtuh menjadi satu sebutan $\\lambda^Q_{x,y} \\langle\\!\\langle G^\\dagger(Q \\otimes I_{N \\cap R} \\otimes Z^x) |$, menghasilkan keputusan yang dikehendaki.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] for development beyond this point: the definition of the PTG, paths through the PTG, and the proof that any properly-defined path corresponds to an experiment.\n"
msgstr "Lihat \\[[5](#id16 \"Zhihan Zhang, Senrui Chen, Yunchao Liu, and Liang Jiang. Generalized Cycle Benchmarking Algorithm for Characterizing Midcircuit Measurements. PRX Quantum, 6(1):010310, 2025. URL: https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310, doi:10.1103/PRXQuantum.6.010310.\")] untuk perkembangan selepas ini: takrifan PTG, laluan melalui PTG, dan bukti bahawa mana-mana laluan yang ditakrifkan dengan betul sepadan dengan satu eksperimen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "References {#references}"
msgstr "Rujukan {#references}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"id17\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[1]\n"
msgstr "\\[1]\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
